Task Manager CLI

Project Reference

Project Name: Task Manager CLI
Type: Command Line Application
Language: Bash (Shell Scripting)
Platform: Linux / Ubuntu
Version Control: Git & GitHub
Containerization: Docker (nginx:alpine)

Description
Task Manager CLI is an interactive terminal-based application built entirely with Bash scripting.
It allows users to manage their daily tasks from the command line with a clean, color-coded interface.
All data is stored locally in a plain text file using a pipe-separated format.

Core Features

Add tasks with title, priority (high / medium / low), and due date
List all tasks or filter by status or priority
Update any field of an existing task (title, priority, due date, status)
Delete tasks with a confirmation step
Search tasks using regular expressions
Display a summary showing count of pending, in-progress, and done tasks
Detect and list overdue tasks automatically based on today's date
Generate a priority report grouped by high, medium, and low
Export all tasks to a CSV file
Sort tasks by priority or due date


Task Fields
FieldAccepted ValuesPriorityhigh / medium / lowStatuspending / in-progress / doneDue DateYYYY-MM-DD

Color System
ColorMeaningRedHigh priorityYellowMedium priorityGreenLow priority / DoneCyanPending / HeadersBlueDue dates

Data Storage
Tasks are saved in a file called tasks.txt using this format:
ID | Title | Priority | Due Date | Status
Example:
1|Buy groceries|high|2026-03-10|pending
2|Fix bug|medium|2026-11-30|in-progress
3|Read book|low|2026-03-15|done

How to Run
git clone https://github.com/habibamegahed/task-manager-cli.git
cd task-manager-cli
chmod +x task_manager.sh
bash task_manager.sh
Run with Docker
docker build -t task-manager .
docker run -it task-manager

